// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/ MPL-2.0
//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  SMC SESSION SWEEP STRATEGY
// =============================================================================
//  Named `mpc_m15_playbook_strategy.pine` until 2026-08-15. The old name said
//  where the direction is read and nothing about what the setup IS, and it
//  carried the `mpc_` prefix of a Pine family this file is not part of. Grep the
//  old name in HISTORY.md and the build notes — the diary entries keep it.
// =============================================================================
//  The five-step SMC continuation model from Lewis Kelly's "This SMC Strategy Is
//  Too Simple to Ignore", written up in
//  education/learned/2026-08-11-smc-strategy-too-simple-to-ignore-1150-trades.md,
//  turned into something the Strategy Tester can score.
//
//    1. DIRECTION   — 15-minute swing structure only. Bearish = LH/LL, bullish
//                     the mirror. Trade with it, never against it.
//    2. LOCATION    — the current session sweeps the PREVIOUS session's high (for
//                     shorts) or low (for longs). London sweeps Asia; New York
//                     sweeps London. This replaces a fib retracement — the video
//                     is explicit that premium/discount was tested and dropped.
//    3. CONFIRMATION— the 1-minute must flip to AGREE with the 15-minute. After
//                     the sweep, wait for a 1m change of character in the trend's
//                     direction. He names this discrepancy as the edge itself.
//    4. POINT OF INTEREST — the nearest UNTOUCHED 5-minute fair value gap on the
//                     far side of price. Limit into it, stop beyond it.
//    5. TARGETS     — TP1 previous day's low/high, TP2 previous week's low/high.
//
//  WHERE THE STRUCTURE ENGINE CAME FROM
//  ------------------------------------
//  The 15m / 1m structure engine below was lifted BYTE-FOR-BYTE from the
//  drawing-free `MTFStruct` port of `SMCStructure.process()` that used to live in
//  `../engines/mpc_m15_playbook.pine`. That indicator was DELETED on 2026-08-15
//  (Aaron's call — it drew a dashboard nobody read and could not be scored), so
//  the only remaining copies of that state machine are this file and the
//  canonical `engines/market_structure/`. Do not paraphrase it; if it has to
//  change, change it against the canonical engine and say so.
//
//  THE PANEL AND THE PALETTE ARE THE HOUSE STANDARD (2026-08-14)
//  ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Inputs use the numbered groups every strategy in this folder uses, so section
//  5 is Entry whichever file you open. The contract, and the rule that decides
//  which section a new toggle goes in, are in `indicators/strategies/CLAUDE.md`.
//  Sections 1, 2, 9 and 12 are ABSENT and the numbering deliberately does not
//  close up, because the number is the address:
//
//    * `1 · Confirmation table` — this strategy reads no JARVIS table. Same
//      reason BOS, D and H4 do not have one.
//    * `9 · Drawing: fibs` — no fibs.
//    * `12 · Debug` — held one per-event Pine Logs line; cut 2026-08-14 on
//      Aaron's call. Everything it said is on the chart, from the same state.
//    * `2 · Market structure` — the four drawing toggles are NOT here, and this
//      is the one honest gap in the standardisation. Every other file runs its
//      engine on the CHART frame, so drawing it is free. This one runs the engine
//      INSIDE `request.security` on the 15m and the 1m, and Pine cannot draw from
//      in there. A chart-frame copy ported in for the drawing would paint the
//      5m's swings while the strategy trades off the 15m's — a chart that
//      disagrees with the file under it, which is worse than no drawing at all.
//      Closing it properly means returning the swing PRICES through the security
//      call and drawing those. That is a feature, not a port. Aaron's call.
//
//  Every colour a TRADE is drawn in is copied from `mpc_strategy.pine`. Change a
//  value by changing it THERE and copying it down, never by picking one here.
//
//  ⚠ THE PANEL ORDER MOVED, SO THE FIRST PASTE COSTS ONE "Reset settings to
//  defaults". TradingView keys saved input values off declaration order within
//  each type, and this pass reordered, retitled and regrouped all of them.
//  ⚠ IN THE SAME VISIT, untick Style → "Trades on chart". It cannot be defaulted
//  from Pine (there is no `strategy()` argument for it) and it comes back ON
//  after any reset. This file draws its own position box, entry triangles and
//  result callout, so leaving TradingView's markers on puts two renderings of one
//  trade on the same candles, at two different exit prices whenever TP1 filled.
//
//  STATUS — read before trusting a number
//  --------------------------------------
//  * Not compiled anywhere but TradingView; there is no local Pine compiler.
//  * No export twin and no Python port, so no `compare_*.py` covers it.
//  * The video's POI is "order block OR fair value gap". Only the GAP is modelled.
//    A gap-only rule takes strictly FEWER setups than he does.
//  * The 1m confirmation is read through `request.security`, so it is observed at
//    the CHART bar's close — up to one chart bar late, never early. Run this on
//    5m for fidelity; 15m buys you more history and a coarser trigger.
//  * TradingView loads a limited amount of 1-minute history. With the confirmation
//    ON, the far end of a long backtest may see no 1m structure at all and simply
//    take no trades there. Check the trade list's FIRST date against the chart's,
//    and read the tester's window as what you asked for, not what arrived.
// =============================================================================

strategy("SMC Session Sweep Strategy", overlay = true, pyramiding = 0,
  initial_capital = 10000, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
  margin_long = 0.2, margin_short = 0.2, slippage = 0,
  max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 2000)

//  THE DRAWING BUDGET — THERE IS NO BUDGET. NOTHING HERE CAPS ITSELF.
//  ------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Aaron, 2026-08-15: "don't cap it at all. It should just stop when it maxes out
//  TradingView's drawing tools." So every object is drawn and NOTHING is ever
//  deleted by this script. The only limit is the `max_*_count = 500` above, which
//  is Pine's own ceiling and the largest it accepts — when it is reached
//  TradingView drops the OLDEST drawing of that type to make room for the newest.
//  The chart therefore extends back exactly as far as it can and then stops,
//  which is the behaviour asked for.
//
//  ⚠ THIS REPLACED HAND-ROLLED PER-FAMILY CAPS AND THAT IS THE RIGHT TRADE, but
//  it is a trade. Those caps evicted in whole drawings — a setup is 1 box + 4
//  lines + 1 label and it left together — whereas TradingView evicts per OBJECT
//  TYPE, oldest first, with no idea which drawing an object belonged to. So at
//  the very left edge of a long chart a setup can dissolve in pieces: its box
//  goes while its stop line is still there. That is the far edge running out, not
//  a bug, and it is confined to the oldest thing on screen.
//
//  ⚠ THE FAMILIES SHARE THE 500 AND THEY COMPETE. Sessions draw 3 boxes a day
//  whatever happens; trades draw 4 boxes each. On a chart with sessions ON, the
//  sessions will be what pushes the oldest position boxes off. **Count trades in
//  the Strategy Tester's list, never off the chart.**



//============================================================================
//  INPUT PANEL — the numbered groups, in the order they appear
//============================================================================
// ⚠ GROUP ORDER IS THE ORDER EACH GROUP'S FIRST INPUT IS DECLARED. Retagging
// `group =` alone cannot move a section; the declarations have to move.
// ⚠ AN INPUT REFERENCED BY ANOTHER INPUT'S `active =` MUST BE DECLARED ABOVE IT.
// `mpc_bos_strategy.pine` broke exactly that in the 2026-08-12 reorder and it
// only showed up on the paste (CE10272). Re-check after any edit here.
//
// 🔴 THE STEP NUMBERS ARE OUT OF THE INPUT TITLES, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC.
// The titles used to read "1 · Direction timeframe", "4 · Zone timeframe" and so
// on — the VIDEO's five steps — while the group headings carry the house
// contract's own numbers. Two numbering systems on one panel: reading down it
// counted 4, 1, 2, 3, 5, 4, 6, which made a strictly ordered strategy look like
// it had no order at all. Aaron, 2026-08-15, reading his own file: "I don't
// understand the strategy that's laid out in this pine right now."
// The step is spelled out in WORDS instead, so the sequence survives being split
// across groups — which it must be, because the contract groups by what a setting
// CHANGES and this model's five steps do not map onto that one-to-one:
//
//     Direction     step 1  → 4 · What arms it
//     Location      step 2  → 4 · What arms it
//     Confirmation  step 3  → 4 · What arms it
//     Point of int. step 4  → 5 · Entry
//     Targets       step 5  → 6 · Stop & targets
//============================================================================
var string G3  = "3 · What trades"
var string G4  = "4 · What arms it"
var string G5  = "5 · Entry"
var string G6  = "6 · Stop & targets"
var string G7  = "7 · Filters"
var string G8  = "8 · Chart annotations"
var string G10 = "10 · Drawing: sessions"
var string G11 = "11 · Drawing: liquidity"
// No `12 · Debug`. The only thing in it was a per-event Pine Logs line, and
// Aaron cut it 2026-08-14: "for events, we don't need that." What it reported —
// which gate refused a setup, and at what price — is on the chart already, in the
// pink SETUP BLOCKED tooltip and the state panel, and those read the SAME
// `sBlk`/`lBlk` the log did. ⚠ The numbering still does not close up: a future
// debug toggle is 12, not 11b.

// ── 3 · What trades ─────────────────────────────────────────────
bool   pbTradeLongs  = input.bool(true,  "Trade longs",  group = G3, inline = "dir", tooltip = "On = long setups may trade. Off = shorts only. A refused side is block code 1, so a disabled direction stays countable rather than invisible.")
bool   pbTradeShorts = input.bool(true,  "Trade shorts", group = G3, inline = "dir")
string execSizeMode  = input.string("Risk % of equity", "Position sizing", options = ["Risk % of equity", "Fixed contracts"], group = G3, tooltip = "Risk % of equity = every trade risks the same FRACTION of the account, so every trade is exactly 1R and the results compound. Fixed contracts = the same quantity every time, whatever the stop distance. ⚠ Under Fixed, a trade with a $2 stop and one with a $20 stop count the same in the win rate and ten times apart in dollars — read R, never net, under that mode.")
float  execRiskPct   = input.float(1.0, "   ↳ Risk % per trade", minval = 0.01, maxval = 100.0, step = 0.25, group = G3, active = execSizeMode == "Risk % of equity", tooltip = "Percent of equity risked to the stop, so every trade is 1R. R is scale-free — measure at a low value first, size after you know the R distribution. ⚠ 10 busts the account on a strategy that sizes by risk ÷ stop distance; that lesson has been learnt twice in this folder already.")
float  execFixedQty  = input.float(1.0, "   ↳ Contracts", minval = 0.01, step = 0.01, group = G3, active = execSizeMode == "Fixed contracts")

// ── 4 · What arms it ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Steps 1-3 of the model: the direction that gates the side, the session whose
// pool has to be taken, and the lower-timeframe shift that confirms it.
string pbDirTf       = input.string("15", "Direction — trend timeframe", options = ["5", "15", "30", "60", "240"], group = G4, tooltip = "The timeframe whose swing structure sets the bias. Only setups in this timeframe's direction are taken. The video uses 15.")
int    pbStructLen   = input.int(15, "   ↳ Structure pivot length", minval = 2, maxval = 50, group = G4, tooltip = "Seeds the structure engine's first swing. After the seed, swings come from the 3-candle pullback rule, so this mostly decides warm-up depth.")
bool   pbTradeLdn    = input.bool(true, "Location — trade London (sweeps the Asian high/low)",   group = G4, tooltip = "London's pool is Asia's high and low, frozen at the London open.")
bool   pbTradeNy     = input.bool(true, "Location — trade New York (sweeps the London high/low)", group = G4, tooltip = "New York's pool is London's high and low, frozen at the New York open. NY wins the overlap — it is the later session, and its pool is whatever London had made by the time it opened.")
bool   pbRequireConf = input.bool(true, "Confirmation — require a lower-timeframe change of character", group = G4, tooltip = "ON: after the sweep, wait for the confirmation timeframe to shift into the direction timeframe's direction. This is the step the video calls the edge. OFF: enter on the sweep alone — expect to be run to the top of the move.")
string pbConfTf      = input.string("1", "   ↳ Confirmation timeframe", options = ["1", "3", "5", "15"], group = G4, active = pbRequireConf, tooltip = "Where the change of character is read. 1 is the video's. Setting it to the chart timeframe removes the discrepancy the setup is built on.")
string pbConfWhen    = input.string("Before the zone (rest a limit)", "   ↳ When the shift must happen", options = ["Before the zone (rest a limit)", "At the zone (enter at market)"], group = G4, active = pbRequireConf, tooltip = "The ORDER of steps 3 and 4, and it is an open question rather than a setting with a known answer. BEFORE = the video's five steps as listed: the shift happens on the retrace, then the nearest untouched zone is found above/below price and a limit rests in it. AT = the standard SMC sequence: the zone is frozen when the sweep completes, price has to travel INTO it, and only a shift that happens while price is inside it counts — then entry is at MARKET. ⚠ Before is odd on its face: the lower timeframe turns against the move and price then has to push FURTHER to reach your order. ⚠ The note this was built from is a transcript of what he SAID, and its own header records that the chart walkthrough was largely missed — so which one his chart actually does is not established. Run both and let the tester decide.")

// ── 5 · Entry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Everything that decides WHICH ZONES EXIST lives here with the entry rules that
// consume them, not in a group named after the object. See the CLAUDE.md.
string pbPoiTf        = input.string("5", "Point of interest — timeframe the zone is found on", options = ["1", "3", "5", "15"], group = G5, tooltip = "Where the entry zone is found. The video uses a 5-minute order block or fair value gap; only the GAP is modelled here, so this file takes strictly fewer setups than he does.")
bool   pbPoiUntouched = input.bool(true, "   ↳ Untouched zones only", group = G5, tooltip = "ON: a gap price has already traded into is skipped — the video's rule (\"they've been traded, they're no longer of interest\"). OFF: any live gap qualifies, which takes more setups at worse prices.")
string execZoneEntry  = input.string("Proximal edge", "Point of interest — where the limit rests in the zone", options = ["Proximal edge", "Midpoint", "Distal edge"], group = G5, tooltip = "Where the limit rests. Proximal = the edge price reaches first (fills most often, widest stop). Distal = the far edge (best price, fills least). Midpoint is the compromise.")
int    execCancelBars = input.int(0, "Cancel an unfilled limit after N bars", minval = 0, maxval = 2000, group = G5, tooltip = "0 = keep it until the session that placed it ends. A resting order is always cancelled at the end of its own session, whatever this says.")
bool   execCancelFlip = input.bool(true, "Cancel on a direction flip or an opposite shift", group = G5, tooltip = "Pulls a resting limit when the direction timeframe turns against it, or the confirmation timeframe shifts the other way. OFF leaves the order in the book against a setup that has stopped being true.")

// ── 6 · Stop & targets ──────────────────────────────────────────
int    execSlBufTk     = input.int(20, "Stop buffer beyond the zone (ticks)", minval = 0, maxval = 500, group = G6, tooltip = "How far past the zone's far edge the stop sits, so a wick through the gap does not take you out.")
bool   execUseTp1      = input.bool(true, "Target 1 — previous day's low / high", group = G6)
bool   execUseTp2      = input.bool(true, "Target 2 — previous week's low / high", group = G6)
float  execTp1Pct      = input.float(50, "   ↳ % banked at the first target", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = G6, tooltip = "0 = bank nothing and ride the whole position to the second target. With only one valid target this is ignored and the whole position exits there. ⚠ Pine reads qty_percent = 0 as UNSPECIFIED and closes the WHOLE position, which is why the rung is skipped rather than issued at 0.")
float  execTpFallbackR = input.float(3.0, "Fallback target (R) when no liquidity target is valid", minval = 0.0, maxval = 50.0, step = 0.5, group = G6, tooltip = "A target on the wrong side of the entry, or nearer than the minimum below, cannot be used. 0 = refuse the setup instead of substituting a fixed R.")
float  execMinRr       = input.float(1.0, "Minimum reward:risk to the first target", minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.25, group = G6, tooltip = "A target closer than this many R is treated as unusable. Entering a hair above the previous day's low is how a 6R model turns into a 0.2R one.")
bool   execBeAtTp1     = input.bool(true, "Stop to breakeven when the first target is reached", group = G6)
int    execBeBufTk     = input.int(20, "   ↳ Breakeven buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, maxval = 500, group = G6, active = execBeAtTp1)
float  execTimeStopHrs = input.float(0.0, "Time stop (hours, 0 = off)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 240.0, step = 1.0, group = G6, tooltip = "Close a trade that has been open this long and has NOT reached its first target. Trades past the first target are left alone — that gate is what stops a clock cutting the winners.")

// ── 7 · Filters — the things that REFUSE a setup ────────────────
string execMinStopMode = input.string("% of price", "Minimum stop distance", options = ["Off", "% of price", "Fixed $", "x ATR(14)"], group = G7, tooltip = "Refuse a setup whose stop lands too close to the entry. Size is risk divided by stop distance, so a stop that collapses onto the entry does not risk less — it builds a huge position.")
float  execMinStopVal  = input.float(0.08, "   ↳ Minimum stop floor (unit = mode above)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 0.01, group = G7, active = execMinStopMode != "Off", tooltip = "The floor itself. The unit follows the setting above — a percent of price, dollars, or an ATR multiple. Higher refuses more setups.")
float  pbPoiMaxAtr     = input.float(0.0, "Maximum distance to the zone (x ATR14)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.5, group = G7, tooltip = "Refuse a zone further from price than this. 0 = no limit. A zone three ATR away is a setup you will rarely be filled on and never at a good stop.")

// ── 8 · Chart annotations ───────────────────────────────────────
bool  execShowPosBox = input.bool(true, "Show position box (result)", group = G8, tooltip = "One box per trade, growing right while it is open, plus the entry triangle. On close it paints the result: green from entry to the exit on a winner, red to the stop fill on a loser, an orange line at entry on a breakeven. Replaces TradingView's built-in trade markers — untick Style → \"Trades on chart\" or you get both. ⚠ Trades are drawn as far back as the chart allows and then stop — TradingView keeps only the newest 500 drawings per script, and turning sessions on takes 3 boxes a day out of that same 500. Count trades in the Strategy Tester's list, never off the chart.")
float execBeBandR    = input.float(0.15, "   ↳ Breakeven band (R)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = G8, active = execShowPosBox, tooltip = "A closed trade whose net result lands inside ± this many R counts as a BREAKEVEN rather than a win or a loss. The breakeven buffer books a few ticks, so without a band the Strategy Tester files every scratch as a winner.")
bool  showSetups     = input.bool(true, "Draw the zone, stop and targets", group = G8, tooltip = "The setup itself, drawn when the limit is placed: the gap as a box, the entry dashed, the stop, and both targets. The stop line follows the LIVE stop, so a staged breakeven is visible on the chart.")
bool  showBlockTag   = input.bool(true, "Mark blocked setups on chart (pink)", group = G8, tooltip = "Drops a pink SETUP BLOCKED tag whenever the sequence reached the zone and one of the gates refused it. Hover for the reason and the price the limit would have rested at. This is how you find out whether a gate is saving you money or costing it: count the tags, flip the gate, re-run, compare. Cosmetic — it never changes a trade.")
int   debugDays      = input.int(30, "   ↳ Only tag the last N days", minval = 1, maxval = 3650, group = G8, active = showBlockTag)
bool  showStatePanel = input.bool(true, "Show the state panel", group = G8, tooltip = "A six-row read of where the sequence has got to. It reports the GATES rather than only the outcome — a quiet market and a rule set too tight look identical from a trade count alone, and they need opposite responses.")

// ── 10 · Drawing: sessions ──────────────────────────────────────
// ONE toggle, default OFF, sub-settings hidden. Aaron, 2026-08-12: "I don't even
// need to see the time frame or the colors of the sessions. It could just be one
// button that says show sessions… I'll never configure them."
bool pbShowSess = input.bool(false, "Show sessions", group = G10, tooltip = "Boxes Tokyo, London and New York round their OWN high and low — not a full-height stripe, because the box's top and bottom ARE the pool the next session hunts. Draw-only: the session WINDOWS decide which pool a sweep is measured against and are frozen at the repo's DST-aware values, so this cannot move a trade. Intraday charts only. ⚠ Sessions are drawn as far back as the chart allows and then stop — TradingView keeps only the newest 500 drawings per script, and these compete with the trade boxes for that 500. The left edge is the limit, not a gap.")

// ── 11 · Drawing: liquidity ─────────────────────────────────────
// ON by default, unlike the other draw toggles, and the reason is that this is
// not decoration: it is STEP 2. The red line is the level a short is waiting to
// see taken and the green one is the long's, so it is the single line that
// explains why the strategy did or did not do anything on a given day.
bool pbShowPool = input.bool(true, "Show the previous session's high / low (the sweep level)", group = G11, tooltip = "London's pool is Asia's high and low; New York's is London's. Frozen at the session open, so the level cannot move under the setup watching it, and drawn only for the session that is hunting it.")

//============================================================
//  SESSION WINDOWS — frozen, not inputs
//============================================================
// The repo's DST-aware windows, identical in every Pine file here since
// 2026-07-31. They are each session's own city clock rather than a fixed GMT
// offset, so a changeover does not silently move the pool a sweep is measured
// against. ⚠ They DECIDE trades — the pool is read from them — so they are
// hardcoded rather than exposed, and a change to one belongs in every file that
// carries this block, not just this one.
string sessAsia = "0900-1800"
string tzAsia   = "Asia/Tokyo"
string sessLdn  = "0800-1700"
string tzLdn    = "Europe/London"
string sessNy   = "0800-1700"
string tzNy     = "America/New_York"

//============================================================
//  THE ANNOTATION PALETTE — copied from mpc_strategy.pine
//============================================================
// One result, one colour, on every chart in this folder. A+ is the standard and
// carries TWO palettes on purpose: the POSITION palette below is every colour a
// TRADE is drawn in, and the TABLE palette further down is the state panel's.
// `mpc_d_strategy.pine` shipped with the table palette on its trades — a winner
// drew in the green A+ uses for a table row — which is the drift this block
// exists to stop. Change a value in A+ first and copy it down.
color POS_WIN    = color.new(#26A69A, 12)  // closed winner — label
color POS_WINL   = color.new(#26A69A, 0)   //              — leader line
color POS_LOSS   = color.new(#EF5350, 12)
color POS_LOSSL  = color.new(#EF5350, 0)
color POS_BE     = color.new(#FF9800, 12)  // inside the band — ORANGE, never yellow
color POS_BEL    = color.new(#FF9800, 0)
color POS_OPEN   = color.new(#787B86, 12)  // result not known yet
color POS_OPENL  = color.new(#787B86, 0)
color POS_OPENBG = color.new(#787B86, 80)  // the live box while the trade runs
color POS_GREENB = color.new(#26A69A, 0)   // solid borders so even a thin box is visible
color POS_REDB   = color.new(#EF5350, 0)
color POS_G1     = color.new(#26A69A, 55)  // reward, by rung — one hue, three depths:
color POS_G2     = color.new(#26A69A, 70)  // the gradient IS the legend, so nothing
color POS_DD     = color.new(#EF5350, 88)  // has to be labelled by colour
color TP_ANNOT   = color.new(#26A69A, 40)  // ONE colour for every target line
color BLK_PINK   = color.new(#FF2E9A, 12)  // blocked setup
color BLK_PINKL  = color.new(#FF2E9A, 0)
color TXT_DARK   = color.new(#101014, 0)   // dark text on every bright fill

// The three session shades, also A+'s. Tokyo red, London blue, New York yellow.
color SESS_ASIA = color.new(#FF5252, 92)
color SESS_LDN  = color.new(#2962FF, 92)
color SESS_NY   = color.new(#FFEB3B, 90)

// The TABLE palette — the state panel only, and deliberately different greens and
// reds from the position palette above. Do not cross them.
color TBL_GOOD = #00E676
color TBL_WARN = #ffde59
color TBL_OFF  = color.new(color.gray, 30)

//============================================================
//  SHARED
//============================================================
float pbBuffer = 0.0
float atr14    = ta.atr(14)
float tickSz   = syminfo.mintick

// Previous day / previous week extremes — the trade's targets. `lookahead_on` with a
// [1] offset is the non-repainting idiom: it asks for the COMPLETED prior period.
[pdh, pdl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwh, pwl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

//============================================================
//  MARKET STRUCTURE ENGINE (drawing-free)
//============================================================
// Lifted BYTE-FOR-BYTE from the MTFStruct block of mpc_m15_playbook.pine (that
// indicator was deleted 2026-08-15; see the header), itself a drawing-free port
// of SMCStructure.process() — the same state machine as
// engines/market_structure/, which is now the only other copy. It runs inside
// request.security so each
// timeframe is tracked on its own bars, independent of the chart timeframe.
// Do not paraphrase or 'tidy' it: a swing map that disagrees with the chart is
// a strategy trading a different market from the one being read.
type MTFStruct
    int    length
    float  ash             = na
    int    ash_loc         = na
    string ash_type        = ""
    float  asl             = na
    int    asl_loc         = na
    string asl_type        = ""
    float  last_conf_high     = na
    int    last_conf_high_loc = na
    float  last_conf_low      = na
    int    last_conf_low_loc  = na
    int    dir            = 0
    bool   choch_lock     = false
    int    pb_mode        = 0
    int    pb_count       = 0
    float  pb_level       = na
    float  pb_extreme     = na
    int    pb_extreme_loc = na
    bool   pb_started     = false
    float  pb_last_qualify_close = na
    float  pb_last_qualify_high  = na
    float  pb_extreme_close      = na
    float  prev_close     = na
    float  prev_high      = na
    float  prev_low       = na
    bool   seeded         = false
    bool   bull_bos       = false
    float  bull_bos_high  = na
    int    bull_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bull_bos_low   = na
    int    bull_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   bear_bos       = false
    float  bear_bos_high  = na
    int    bear_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bear_bos_low   = na
    int    bear_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   new_swing_high = false
    bool   new_swing_low  = false
    bool   bull_sos       = false
    bool   bear_sos       = false

method mtfCreateAsh(MTFStruct st, float val, int loc) =>
    st.ash      := val
    st.ash_loc  := loc
    st.ash_type := ""

method mtfCreateAsl(MTFStruct st, float val, int loc) =>
    st.asl      := val
    st.asl_loc  := loc
    st.asl_type := ""

// Byte-for-byte the state logic of SMCStructure.process(); drawing removed.
method processMTF(MTFStruct st, float ph_val, float pl_val) =>
    st.bull_bos := false
    st.bear_bos := false
    st.new_swing_high := false
    st.new_swing_low  := false
    st.bull_sos := false
    st.bear_sos := false

    bool is_inside = false
    if not na(st.prev_high) and not na(st.prev_low)
        is_inside := high < st.prev_high and low > st.prev_low

    if st.choch_lock
        if st.dir == 1 and not na(pl_val)
            st.choch_lock := false
        else if st.dir == -1 and not na(ph_val)
            st.choch_lock := false

    if st.pb_mode == 1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or high > st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := high
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_1        := true
            bool extreme_is_bearish_1 = extreme_updated_1 and close < open
            bool is_candle1_1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_1) and (not extreme_updated_1 or extreme_is_bearish_1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close < threshold - pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := low
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
                st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
                st.new_swing_high := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    else if st.pb_mode == -1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_m1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or low < st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := low
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_m1       := true
            bool extreme_is_bullish_m1 = extreme_updated_m1 and close > open
            bool is_candle1_m1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_m1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_m1) and (not extreme_updated_m1 or extreme_is_bullish_m1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close > threshold + pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := high
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
                st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
                st.new_swing_low := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    st.prev_close := close
    st.prev_high  := high
    st.prev_low   := low

    if na(st.ash) and na(st.asl) and not st.seeded
        if not na(ph_val)
            st.mtfCreateAsh(ph_val, bar_index[st.length])
            st.dir := -1
        else if not na(pl_val)
            st.mtfCreateAsl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length])
            st.dir := 1

    if not st.seeded
        if not na(st.ash) and na(st.asl)
            float seed_low = low
            int   seed_loc = bar_index
            int   lb       = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if low[i] < seed_low
                    seed_low := low[i]
                    seed_loc := bar_index - i
            if seed_low < st.ash
                st.asl      := seed_low
                st.asl_loc  := seed_loc
                st.asl_type := ""
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.asl) and na(st.ash)
            float seed_high = high
            int   seed_loc  = bar_index
            int   lb        = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if high[i] > seed_high
                    seed_high := high[i]
                    seed_loc  := bar_index - i
            if seed_high > st.asl
                st.ash      := seed_high
                st.ash_loc  := seed_loc
                st.ash_type := ""
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.ash) and not na(st.asl)
            st.seeded := true

    if na(st.last_conf_high) and na(st.last_conf_low)
        if not na(ph_val) and not na(st.ash) and st.ash_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if ph_val > st.ash
                st.mtfCreateAsh(ph_val, bar_index[st.length])
        if not na(pl_val) and not na(st.asl) and st.asl_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if pl_val < st.asl
                st.mtfCreateAsl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length])

    bool ash_broken = not na(st.ash) and close > st.ash
    bool asl_broken = not na(st.asl) and close < st.asl

    if ash_broken
        st.bull_bos := true
        st.bull_bos_high  := st.ash
        st.bull_bos_h_loc := st.ash_loc

        bool was_in_bear_pb = st.pb_mode == -1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool is_choch = st.dir == -1
        if is_choch
            st.bull_sos := true
            st.choch_lock := true

        st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
        st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
        st.ash                := na
        st.dir                := 1

        if was_in_bear_pb
            st.bull_bos_low   := st.pb_extreme
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
            st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_low     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_low_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            if not na(st.asl)
                bool already_conf_low = (st.asl == st.last_conf_low and st.asl_loc == st.last_conf_low_loc)
                if not already_conf_low
                    st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
                    st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
                st.asl      := na

            float lowest_val = low
            int   lowest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back  = na(st.last_conf_high_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_high_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if low[i] < lowest_val
                        lowest_val := low[i]
                        lowest_loc := bar_index - i

            st.bull_bos_low   := lowest_val
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := lowest_loc

            st.asl      := lowest_val
            st.asl_loc  := lowest_loc
            st.asl_type := ""

            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

    else if asl_broken
        st.bear_bos := true
        st.bear_bos_low   := st.asl
        st.bear_bos_l_loc := st.asl_loc

        bool was_in_bull_pb = st.pb_mode == 1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool is_choch = st.dir == 1
        if is_choch
            st.bear_sos := true
            st.choch_lock := true

        st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
        st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
        st.asl               := na
        st.dir               := -1

        if was_in_bull_pb
            st.bear_bos_high  := st.pb_extreme
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
            st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_high     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_high_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            float highest_val = high
            int   highest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back   = na(st.last_conf_low_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_low_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if high[i] > highest_val
                        highest_val := high[i]
                        highest_loc := bar_index - i

            if not na(st.ash)
                bool already_conf_high = (st.ash == st.last_conf_high and st.ash_loc == st.last_conf_high_loc)
                if not already_conf_high
                    st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
                st.ash      := na
            else
                if highest_val != st.last_conf_high
                    st.last_conf_high     := highest_val
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := highest_loc

            st.bear_bos_high  := highest_val
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := highest_loc

            st.ash      := highest_val
            st.ash_loc  := highest_loc
            st.ash_type := ""

            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

//============================================================
//  STEP 1 — DIRECTION, and STEP 3 — CONFIRMATION
//============================================================
// One wrapper over the engine above, run on two timeframes. The body executes on
// EVERY bar of the requested timeframe — so on a 5m chart asking for "1", this
// state machine steps through all five 1-minute bars inside each chart bar. What
// crosses back is only the value as at the LAST of them.
//
// 🔴 WHICH IS WHY IT RETURNS A COUNTER AND NOT `mtf.bull_sos`. `processMTF` clears
// that flag at the top of every bar and sets it only on the bar that shifted, so
// sampling it once per chart bar reads the FIFTH 1-minute bar and nothing else —
// a change of character on 1-minute bars one through four is invisible, which is
// four fifths of them. The counter accumulates inside the chart bar, so diffing
// it against the previous chart bar catches a shift wherever it happened.
// ⚠ An earlier version of this comment justified the counter by saying a flag
// "stays true" through `request.security`. That is the opposite of the real
// failure — it goes STALE-FALSE, not stale-true — and the code was right for a
// reason its own comment got wrong.
// ⚠ The cost that remains: the shift is known at the chart bar's CLOSE. Up to one
// chart bar late, never early, which is the safe direction.
f_pbStruct(int len) =>
    var mtf = MTFStruct.new(length = len)
    var int shifts = 0
    float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, len, len)
    float pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  len, len)
    mtf.processMTF(ph, pl)
    if mtf.bull_sos or mtf.bear_sos
        shifts += 1
    [mtf.dir, shifts]

[dirDir,  dirShifts]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, pbDirTf,  f_pbStruct(pbStructLen))
[confDir, confShifts] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, pbConfTf, f_pbStruct(pbStructLen))

bool newConfShift = not na(confShifts) and not na(confShifts[1]) and confShifts > confShifts[1]

//============================================================
//  STEP 2 — LOCATION: the previous session's high or low, taken
//============================================================
bool inAsia = not na(time("", sessAsia, tzAsia))
bool inLdn  = not na(time("", sessLdn,  tzLdn))
bool inNy   = not na(time("", sessNy,   tzNy))

var float asiaHi = na, var float asiaLo = na
var float ldnHi  = na, var float ldnLo  = na
if inAsia
    asiaHi := (not inAsia[1] or na(asiaHi)) ? high : math.max(asiaHi, high)
    asiaLo := (not inAsia[1] or na(asiaLo)) ? low  : math.min(asiaLo, low)
if inLdn
    ldnHi := (not inLdn[1] or na(ldnHi)) ? high : math.max(ldnHi, high)
    ldnLo := (not inLdn[1] or na(ldnLo)) ? low  : math.min(ldnLo, low)

// New York wins the overlap — it is the later session, and its pool is whatever
// London had made by the time it opened. The pool is FROZEN at the session open
// rather than read live, so the level a sweep is measured against cannot move
// under the setup that is watching it.
int  rawSess     = inNy ? 2 : inLdn ? 1 : 0
bool sessTradable = rawSess == 2 ? pbTradeNy : rawSess == 1 ? pbTradeLdn : false
bool newLeg      = rawSess != rawSess[1]

var float  poolHi = na, var float poolLo = na
var string poolNm = ""
var int    legId  = 0
if newLeg
    legId += 1
    if rawSess == 1
        poolHi := asiaHi
        poolLo := asiaLo
        poolNm := "Asia"
    else if rawSess == 2
        poolHi := ldnHi
        poolLo := ldnLo
        poolNm := "London"
    else
        poolHi := na
        poolLo := na
        poolNm := ""

var bool sweptHi = false, var bool sweptLo = false
var bool confShort = false, var bool confLong = false
var bool tookLeg = false
if newLeg
    sweptHi   := false
    sweptLo   := false
    confShort := false
    confLong  := false
    tookLeg   := false

// The BAR and the LEVEL are recorded at the moment the sweep latches, so the
// chart can draw the level that was taken instead of writing its name. They are
// captured on the first bar only — a level is taken once, and re-stamping it
// every bar price stayed through would move the mark away from the event.
var int   sweepHiBar = na, var float sweepHiLvl = na
var int   sweepLoBar = na, var float sweepLoLvl = na
if rawSess != 0
    if not na(poolHi) and high > poolHi
        if not sweptHi
            sweepHiBar := bar_index
            sweepHiLvl := poolHi
        sweptHi := true
    if not na(poolLo) and low < poolLo
        if not sweptLo
            sweepLoBar := bar_index
            sweepLoLvl := poolLo
        sweptLo := true


//============================================================
//  STEP 4 — POINT OF INTEREST: the nearest untouched gap
//============================================================
// Runs the 3-candle imbalance rule on the zone timeframe and returns the nearest
// LIVE gap on each side of price. "Untouched" is tracked explicitly: a gap price
// has already traded into is still alive (it dies only on a close fully past it),
// and the video skips exactly those.
f_poiScan(bool untouchedOnly) =>
    var array<float> zTop  = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> zBot  = array.new<float>()
    var array<bool>  zBull = array.new<bool>()
    var array<bool>  zTap  = array.new<bool>()
    var array<int>   zBorn = array.new<int>()
    float thr = timeframe.in_seconds() < 900 ? 0.0 : 0.04
    if barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index >= 2
        bool bull = low > high[2] and (low - high[2]) / high[2] * 100 > thr
        bool bear = high < low[2] and (low[2] - high) / low[2] * 100 > thr
        if bull
            array.push(zTop, low)
            array.push(zBot, high[2])
            array.push(zBull, true)
            array.push(zTap, false)
            array.push(zBorn, bar_index)
        if bear
            array.push(zTop, low[2])
            array.push(zBot, high)
            array.push(zBull, false)
            array.push(zTap, false)
            array.push(zBorn, bar_index)
        while array.size(zTop) > 30
            array.shift(zTop)
            array.shift(zBot)
            array.shift(zBull)
            array.shift(zTap)
            array.shift(zBorn)
        if array.size(zTop) > 0
            for i = array.size(zTop) - 1 to 0
                float t   = array.get(zTop, i)
                float b   = array.get(zBot, i)
                bool  isB = array.get(zBull, i)
                bool  aged = bar_index > array.get(zBorn, i)
                if aged and (isB ? close <= b : close >= t)
                    array.remove(zTop, i)
                    array.remove(zBot, i)
                    array.remove(zBull, i)
                    array.remove(zTap, i)
                    array.remove(zBorn, i)
                else if aged and high >= b and low <= t
                    array.set(zTap, i, true)
    float bullT = na
    float bullB = na
    float bearT = na
    float bearB = na
    if array.size(zTop) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(zTop) - 1
            float t = array.get(zTop, i)
            float b = array.get(zBot, i)
            bool ok = not untouchedOnly or not array.get(zTap, i)
            if ok
                if array.get(zBull, i) and t < close
                    if na(bullT) or t > bullT
                        bullT := t
                        bullB := b
                if not array.get(zBull, i) and b > close
                    if na(bearB) or b < bearB
                        bearT := t
                        bearB := b
    [bullT, bullB, bearT, bearB]

[poiBullTop, poiBullBot, poiBearTop, poiBearBot] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, pbPoiTf, f_poiScan(pbPoiUntouched))

// ── STEPS 3 AND 4, IN EITHER ORDER ──────────────────────────────
// `pbConfWhen` decides which happens first, and it is an OPEN QUESTION rather
// than a setting with a right answer. Aaron, 2026-08-15: "why would I look for
// the gap after a one-minute shift? Shouldn't I look for the point of interest
// first, and then once price is in it, look for the shift?" He is describing the
// standard SMC sequence, and the objection is a good one: under the video's
// listed order the lower timeframe turns AGAINST the move and price then has to
// push FURTHER to reach the resting order.
// ⚠ The note this was built from is a transcript of what he SAID, and its own
// header records that frame selection largely missed the chart walkthrough — so
// the five steps' ORDER is established and the mechanics are not. Neither branch
// here is the "correct" one. Run both.
//
// AT THE ZONE — the zone is FROZEN when the sweep completes, because the live
// scan would drop it at the worst possible moment: a gap price has traded into is
// marked touched, and with untouched-only on it stops being returned exactly as
// price arrives. `armDir` is stored with it so a direction flip mid-session
// cannot hand a bear zone to a long.
bool confAtZone = pbRequireConf and pbConfWhen == "At the zone (enter at market)"

var float armZTop = na, var float armZBot = na
var int   armDir  = 0
var bool  armTouched = false
if newLeg
    armZTop := na
    armZBot := na
    armDir  := 0
    armTouched := false

if confAtZone and rawSess != 0
    if armDir == 0
        if dirDir == -1 and sweptHi and not na(poiBearTop)
            armZTop := poiBearTop
            armZBot := poiBearBot
            armDir  := -1
        else if dirDir == 1 and sweptLo and not na(poiBullTop)
            armZTop := poiBullTop
            armZBot := poiBullBot
            armDir  := 1
    if not na(armZTop) and high >= armZBot and low <= armZTop
        armTouched := true

// A shift only counts as confirmation once the sweep has happened — the sequence
// is location THEN confirmation, and a 1m flip before the sweep is a different
// setup wearing the same flag. In AT-THE-ZONE mode it must ALSO happen while
// price is inside the frozen zone.
if rawSess != 0 and newConfShift
    bool placeOk = not confAtZone or armTouched
    if sweptHi and confDir == -1 and placeOk
        confShort := true
    if sweptLo and confDir == 1 and placeOk
        confLong := true

bool confOkShort = pbRequireConf ? confShort : sweptHi
bool confOkLong  = pbRequireConf ? confLong  : sweptLo

//============================================================
//  STEP 5 — TARGETS
//============================================================
// TP1 is the previous day's extreme, TP2 the previous week's. Which of the two is
// nearer is a fact about the week, not a constant, so they are ORDERED by distance
// rather than assumed. A target on the wrong side of the entry, or nearer than the
// minimum reward, is not a target — it is refused or replaced by the fallback,
// never quietly used.
f_targets(int dir, float entry, float dist) =>
    float a = dir == 1 ? (execUseTp1 ? pdh : na) : (execUseTp1 ? pdl : na)
    float b = dir == 1 ? (execUseTp2 ? pwh : na) : (execUseTp2 ? pwl : na)
    float minDist = execMinRr * dist
    bool aOk = not na(a) and (dir == 1 ? a - entry >= minDist : entry - a >= minDist)
    bool bOk = not na(b) and (dir == 1 ? b - entry >= minDist : entry - b >= minDist)
    float t1 = na
    float t2 = na
    if aOk and bOk
        float da = math.abs(a - entry)
        float db = math.abs(b - entry)
        t1 := da <= db ? a : b
        t2 := da <= db ? b : a
        if math.abs(t2 - t1) < dist * 0.25
            t2 := na
    else if aOk
        t1 := a
    else if bOk
        t1 := b
    if na(t1) and execTpFallbackR > 0
        t1 := dir == 1 ? entry + execTpFallbackR * dist : entry - execTpFallbackR * dist
    [t1, t2]

//============================================================
//  STATE
//============================================================
var int   pendDir   = 0
var float pendEntry = na, var float pendStop = na
var float pendT1    = na, var float pendT2   = na
var float pendZTop  = na, var float pendZBot = na
var int   pendBar   = na

var int   posDir    = 0
var float posEntry  = na, var float posStop = na
var float posT1     = na, var float posT2   = na
var float posZTop   = na, var float posZBot = na
var float posDist   = na, var float posQty  = na
var int   posTime   = na
var float pnlAtFill = 0.0
var bool  t1Done    = false
// The worst price the trade actually SAW. Not the stop — the stop is where it
// would have died, and drawing that as if price went there is the same lie as
// drawing a target it never reached.
var float posWorst  = na

float minStopDist = execMinStopMode == "% of price" ? close * execMinStopVal / 100 : execMinStopMode == "Fixed $" ? execMinStopVal : execMinStopMode == "x ATR(14)" ? (na(atr14) ? 0.0 : atr14 * execMinStopVal) : 0.0

//============================================================
//  CANCEL A RESTING LIMIT
//============================================================
// Before arming, so a session that has just rolled cannot leave the previous
// session's order sitting in the book against a pool nobody is watching.
// `justCancelled` is carried down to the drawing section, which cannot be read
// from up here: a cancelled setup that still looks exactly like a taken one is
// how a chart ends up showing a sweep next to a trade that had nothing to do
// with it.
bool justCancelled = false
if pendDir != 0 and strategy.position_size == 0
    bool cTtl  = execCancelBars > 0 and not na(pendBar) and bar_index - pendBar > execCancelBars
    bool cLeg  = newLeg
    bool cFlip = execCancelFlip and (pendDir == -1 ? dirDir != -1 : dirDir != 1)
    bool cOpp  = execCancelFlip and newConfShift and confDir == -pendDir
    if cTtl or cLeg or cFlip or cOpp
        strategy.cancel(pendDir == -1 ? "PB-S" : "PB-L")
        pendDir := 0
        justCancelled := true

//============================================================
//  THE SETUP — one gate chain per side, first refusal wins
//============================================================
bool flat = strategy.position_size == 0
bool busy = not flat or pendDir != 0 or tookLeg

// The PROXIMAL edge is the one price reaches first, which is the bottom of a zone
// above price and the top of a zone below it — so this cannot be written without
// the direction. Getting it the other way round rests every long at the far edge.
f_zoneEntry(int dir, float zTop, float zBot) =>
    float prox = dir == 1 ? zTop : zBot
    float dist = dir == 1 ? zBot : zTop
    execZoneEntry == "Proximal edge" ? prox : execZoneEntry == "Distal edge" ? dist : (zTop + zBot) / 2

// ── SHORT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// In AT-THE-ZONE mode the zone is the FROZEN one and the entry is at MARKET:
// price is already inside the zone, so a limit at its proximal edge would sit
// behind the market and fill instantly anyway. `close` is the sizing estimate;
// the real fill is read back off the position at `justFilled`.
float sZTop  = confAtZone ? (armDir == -1 ? armZTop : na) : poiBearTop
float sZBot  = confAtZone ? (armDir == -1 ? armZBot : na) : poiBearBot
float sEntry = na(sZTop) ? na : confAtZone ? close : f_zoneEntry(-1, sZTop, sZBot)
float sStop  = na(sZTop) ? na : sZTop + execSlBufTk * tickSz
float sDist  = na(sEntry) or na(sStop) ? na : sStop - sEntry
[sT1, sT2]   = f_targets(-1, nz(sEntry, close), nz(sDist, close * 0.001))

int sBlk = 0
if not pbTradeShorts
    sBlk := 1
else if dirDir != -1
    sBlk := 2
else if rawSess == 0 or not sessTradable
    sBlk := 3
else if not sweptHi
    sBlk := 4
else if not confOkShort
    sBlk := 5
else if na(sZTop) or na(sEntry) or (not confAtZone and sEntry <= close)
    sBlk := 6
else if not confAtZone and pbPoiMaxAtr > 0 and not na(atr14) and sEntry - close > pbPoiMaxAtr * atr14
    sBlk := 7
else if na(sDist) or sDist <= 0 or sDist < minStopDist
    sBlk := 8
else if na(sT1)
    sBlk := 9
else if busy
    sBlk := 10

// ── LONG ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
float lZTop  = confAtZone ? (armDir == 1 ? armZTop : na) : poiBullTop
float lZBot  = confAtZone ? (armDir == 1 ? armZBot : na) : poiBullBot
float lEntry = na(lZTop) ? na : confAtZone ? close : f_zoneEntry(1, lZTop, lZBot)
float lStop  = na(lZBot) ? na : lZBot - execSlBufTk * tickSz
float lDist  = na(lEntry) or na(lStop) ? na : lEntry - lStop
[lT1, lT2]   = f_targets(1, nz(lEntry, close), nz(lDist, close * 0.001))

int lBlk = 0
if not pbTradeLongs
    lBlk := 1
else if dirDir != 1
    lBlk := 2
else if rawSess == 0 or not sessTradable
    lBlk := 3
else if not sweptLo
    lBlk := 4
else if not confOkLong
    lBlk := 5
else if na(lZTop) or na(lEntry) or (not confAtZone and lEntry >= close)
    lBlk := 6
else if not confAtZone and pbPoiMaxAtr > 0 and not na(atr14) and close - lEntry > pbPoiMaxAtr * atr14
    lBlk := 7
else if na(lDist) or lDist <= 0 or lDist < minStopDist
    lBlk := 8
else if na(lT1)
    lBlk := 9
else if busy
    lBlk := 10

f_blkWhy(int code) =>
    switch code
        1  => "that direction is switched off"
        2  => "the direction timeframe is not on this side"
        3  => "outside a session that trades"
        4  => "the previous session's level has not been taken"
        5  => "no change of character on the confirmation timeframe yet"
        6  => "no untouched zone left on the far side of price"
        7  => "the zone is further from price than the limit allows"
        8  => "the stop is too tight for the minimum-distance guard"
        9  => "no target far enough away to be worth taking"
        10 => "already holding, already resting an order, or already traded this session"
        => ""

//============================================================
//  ENTRY — freeze the zone, then rest the limit
//============================================================
// Everything the trade is priced off is snapshotted HERE. A gap keeps its edges
// but the SELECTION moves as price does, so re-reading it at the fill would rest
// the order against one zone and stop it against another.
bool armShort = sBlk == 0
bool armLong  = lBlk == 0

// Under `Risk % of equity` every trade is exactly 1R, which is what makes the R
// column on the chart mean one thing across the whole run. `Fixed contracts` is
// there to reproduce another script, not because it is better.
f_qty(float dist) =>
    execSizeMode == "Fixed contracts" ? execFixedQty : dist > 0 ? (strategy.equity * execRiskPct / 100) / dist : 0.0

if armShort
    float q = f_qty(sDist)
    if q > 0
        if confAtZone
            strategy.entry("PB-S", strategy.short, qty = q)
        else
            strategy.entry("PB-S", strategy.short, qty = q, limit = sEntry)
        pendDir   := -1
        pendEntry := sEntry
        pendStop  := sStop
        pendT1    := sT1
        pendT2    := sT2
        pendZTop  := sZTop
        pendZBot  := sZBot
        pendBar   := bar_index

if armLong and pendDir == 0
    float q = f_qty(lDist)
    if q > 0
        if confAtZone
            strategy.entry("PB-L", strategy.long, qty = q)
        else
            strategy.entry("PB-L", strategy.long, qty = q, limit = lEntry)
        pendDir   := 1
        pendEntry := lEntry
        pendStop  := lStop
        pendT1    := lT1
        pendT2    := lT2
        pendZTop  := lZTop
        pendZBot  := lZBot
        pendBar   := bar_index

//============================================================
//  FILL, STAGED STOP, EXITS
//============================================================
bool justFilled = strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0
bool justClosed = strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0

if justFilled
    posDir    := strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : -1
    posEntry  := strategy.opentrades.entry_price(strategy.opentrades - 1)
    posStop   := pendStop
    posT1     := pendT1
    posT2     := pendT2
    posZTop   := pendZTop
    posZBot   := pendZBot
    posQty    := math.abs(strategy.position_size)
    posDist   := math.abs(posStop - posEntry)
    posTime   := time
    pnlAtFill := strategy.netprofit
    t1Done    := false
    tookLeg   := true
    posWorst  := posEntry
    pendDir   := 0

// Track the real adverse excursion every bar the trade is open, including the
// fill bar's own remainder.
if strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(posWorst)
    posWorst := posDir == 1 ? math.min(posWorst, low) : math.max(posWorst, high)

// The FILL BAR may not stage its own stop. A resting limit is reached by price
// coming to it from the wrong side, so the fill bar's favourable extreme is the
// approach to the order, not a move the trade made.
if strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0 and not t1Done and not na(posT1)
    if posDir == 1 ? high >= posT1 : low <= posT1
        t1Done := true
        if execBeAtTp1
            posStop := posDir == 1 ? math.max(posStop, posEntry + execBeBufTk * tickSz) : math.min(posStop, posEntry - execBeBufTk * tickSz)

bool twoLegs  = not na(posT2) and execTp1Pct > 0 and execTp1Pct < 100
float runTgt  = twoLegs ? posT2 : posT1
bool  timeUp  = execTimeStopHrs > 0 and not t1Done and not na(posTime) and time - posTime >= execTimeStopHrs * 3600000

// A rung is issued only while it is unfilled: calling strategy.exit again with an
// id whose order has already FILLED places a NEW order rather than modifying it,
// which banks another slice of the remainder every bar.
if strategy.position_size > 0
    if twoLegs and not t1Done
        strategy.exit("L-TP1", from_entry = "PB-L", qty_percent = execTp1Pct, limit = posT1, stop = posStop)
    strategy.exit("L-RUN", from_entry = "PB-L", limit = runTgt, stop = posStop)
    if timeUp
        strategy.close("PB-L", comment = "time stop")

if strategy.position_size < 0
    if twoLegs and not t1Done
        strategy.exit("S-TP1", from_entry = "PB-S", qty_percent = execTp1Pct, limit = posT1, stop = posStop)
    strategy.exit("S-RUN", from_entry = "PB-S", limit = runTgt, stop = posStop)
    if timeUp
        strategy.close("PB-S", comment = "time stop")

float closedR = na
if justClosed
    float pnl = strategy.netprofit - pnlAtFill
    float riskUsd = posDist * posQty
    closedR := riskUsd > 0 ? pnl / riskUsd : na

//============================================================
//  DRAWING — sessions and the pool
//============================================================
// 🔴 A SESSION IS A BOX ROUND ITS OWN RANGE, NEVER A FULL-HEIGHT STRIPE.
// This shipped as `bgcolor()` on 2026-08-14 and Aaron caught it the same day:
// "sessions take up the full vertical zone instead of tracking where the candles
// are, like every other session setting I have." He is right, and it is not only
// cosmetic — the box's TOP AND BOTTOM ARE THE POOL. What London sweeps is the top
// of Asia's box, so a stripe hides the one thing the shading could have shown.
// Same shape as `mpc_strategy.pine`'s SessionInfo: dotted border at @40 and the
// fill at the session's own colour.
// ⚠ NO NAME LABEL ON THE BOX. Aaron, 2026-08-15: "take off the names, I already
// know what the colours are." Red is Asia, blue is London, yellow is New York —
// the same three shades every strategy in this folder uses, so the colour IS the
// name once you have seen one chart. Three labels a day was the single largest
// source of text on this chart and none of it said anything the fill did not.
type SessBox
    box   bx     = na
    float hi     = na
    float lo     = na
    bool  active = false

// 🔴 NOTHING IS EVICTED HERE — see the drawing-budget note at the top of the
// file. This block first shipped capped at 30 boxes, which is 3 a day and so TEN
// TRADING DAYS: the sessions stopped dead at 2026-08-03 while every other drawing
// ran back further, and Aaron found it by looking at the chart. **A self-imposed
// cap that truncates history is indistinguishable from a bug in the thing being
// drawn.** Raising it only moved the mystery, so it is gone: draw everything and
// let TradingView's own 500-object ceiling be the edge.
f_sessDraw(SessBox s, bool inSess, color col) =>
    if inSess
        if not s.active
            s.active := true
            s.hi     := high
            s.lo     := low
            s.bx     := box.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, low, bgcolor = col, border_color = color.new(col, 40), border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dotted)
        else
            s.hi := math.max(s.hi, high)
            s.lo := math.min(s.lo, low)
        box.set_right(s.bx, bar_index)
        box.set_top(s.bx, s.hi)
        box.set_bottom(s.bx, s.lo)
    else
        // Only the LATCH is cleared. The box is left exactly as the session ended
        // — it is the pool the next session will hunt, and deleting it here would
        // erase the level the strategy is about to trade against.
        s.active := false
    int _r = 0

var SessBox sbAsia = SessBox.new()
var SessBox sbLdn  = SessBox.new()
var SessBox sbNy   = SessBox.new()
if pbShowSess and timeframe.isintraday
    f_sessDraw(sbAsia, inAsia, SESS_ASIA)
    f_sessDraw(sbLdn,  inLdn,  SESS_LDN)
    f_sessDraw(sbNy,   inNy,   SESS_NY)

plot(pbShowPool and rawSess != 0 ? poolHi : na, "Pool high", color = POS_REDB,   style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(pbShowPool and rawSess != 0 ? poolLo : na, "Pool low",  color = POS_GREENB, style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)

//============================================================
//  DRAWING — the setup, and the trade it became
//============================================================
// Two object families. Only the CURRENT one of each is held in a variable, and
// that is all these handles are for — extending the box while the trade runs,
// following the stop as it stages, recolouring the label on the close. Once a
// drawing is finished it is never touched again and never deleted; TradingView's
// 500-object ceiling is the only thing that removes anything. See the top of the
// file for what that costs at the far-left edge.
var box   curBox = na
var line  curEnt = na
var line  curStp = na
var line  curT1  = na
var line  curT2  = na
var line  curSwp = na
var box   pRisk = na
var box   pRwd1 = na
var box   pRwd2 = na
var box   pBody = na
var line  pLead = na
var label pLbl  = na
// ── the setup, drawn on the bar the limit is placed ─────────────
bool armedNow   = pendDir != 0 and pendBar == bar_index
bool armedShort = armedNow and pendDir == -1
if showSetups and armedNow
    float zt = pendZTop
    float zb = pendZBot
    color c  = armedShort ? POS_REDB : POS_GREENB
    curBox := box.new(bar_index, math.max(zt, zb), bar_index + 12, math.min(zt, zb), border_color = c, border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(c, 88))
    curEnt := line.new(bar_index, pendEntry, bar_index + 12, pendEntry, color = POS_OPENL, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
    curStp := line.new(bar_index, pendStop,  bar_index + 12, pendStop,  color = POS_REDB,  style = line.style_solid, width = 1)
    curT1  := na(pendT1) ? line(na) : line.new(bar_index, pendT1, bar_index + 12, pendT1, color = TP_ANNOT, style = line.style_solid,  width = 1)
    curT2  := na(pendT2) ? line(na) : line.new(bar_index, pendT2, bar_index + 12, pendT2, color = TP_ANNOT, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
    // 🔴 THE SWEPT LEVEL IS DRAWN, NOT NAMED. This used to be a label reading
    // "London sweep" / "Asia sweep" on every armed setup, and it was pure noise:
    // a trade can ONLY exist here if a sweep happened, so the words restated the
    // trade's own existence, while stacking a second text box on top of the
    // result label. Aaron, 2026-08-15: "if it took a long or a short, I'm
    // assuming it's because there was a sweep — just draw the level swept, so I
    // can understand why it won or lost."
    // What replaces it carries information the label never did: WHICH price was
    // taken and WHEN, drawn from the sweep bar across to the setup. Dashed and
    // double width so it cannot be read as the stop, which is solid and thin.
    float swLvl = armedShort ? sweepHiLvl : sweepLoLvl
    int   swBar = armedShort ? sweepHiBar : sweepLoBar
    curSwp := na(swLvl) or na(swBar) ? line(na) : line.new(swBar, swLvl, bar_index + 12, swLvl, color = armedShort ? POS_REDB : POS_GREENB, style = line.style_dashed, width = 2)

// Extend the live setup while its order rests or its position is open.
if showSetups and (pendDir != 0 or strategy.position_size != 0) and not na(curBox)
    box.set_right(curBox, bar_index + 2)
    line.set_x2(curEnt, bar_index + 2)
    line.set_x2(curStp, bar_index + 2)
    if not na(curT1)
        line.set_x2(curT1, bar_index + 2)
    if not na(curT2)
        line.set_x2(curT2, bar_index + 2)
    if not na(curSwp)
        line.set_x2(curSwp, bar_index + 2)
    // The stop line follows the LIVE stop, so a staged breakeven is visible.
    if strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(posStop)
        line.set_y1(curStp, posStop)
        line.set_y2(curStp, posStop)

// 🔴 A CANCELLED SETUP IS GREYED AND RENAMED, AND NOT DOING THAT WAS THE SECOND
// HALF OF THE SAME CONFUSION. Most armed setups never fill — the session rolls,
// the direction flips, price never comes back to the zone — and every one of them
// used to leave a full-colour "London sweep" label with its zone, stop and both
// targets, identical in every way to a setup that traded. So a chart could show a
// green LONG sweep sitting beside a red SHORT result and there was no way to see
// that they were different setups and only one of them ever became a trade.
// ⚠ THE ONLY TEXT A SETUP EVER GETS, AND IT APPEARS ONLY WHEN THE SETUP DIED.
// An armed setup draws no label at all now — a filled one is already named by the
// result label, and stacking a second box of text on the same candles is what
// made this chart unreadable. A CANCELLED one has nothing else to speak for it,
// so it gets a small grey mark and everything it drew is faded to match.
if showSetups and justCancelled and not na(curBox)
    box.set_bgcolor(curBox, color.new(color.gray, 95))
    box.set_border_color(curBox, POS_OPENL)
    line.set_color(curEnt, POS_OPENL)
    line.set_color(curStp, POS_OPENL)
    if not na(curT1)
        line.set_color(curT1, POS_OPENL)
    if not na(curT2)
        line.set_color(curT2, POS_OPENL)
    if not na(curSwp)
        line.set_color(curSwp, POS_OPENL)
    label.new(bar_index, curBox.get_top(), "✕", style = label.style_label_down, color = POS_OPEN, textcolor = TXT_DARK, size = size.tiny, tooltip = "This setup armed and the order was pulled before it filled.\nIt is NOT the trade drawn near it.")

// ── the position, born on the fill and graded on the close ──────
// Grey while it is open, because the result is not known yet. Direction is
// already carried by the arrow, the word, and the entry triangle.
if execShowPosBox and justFilled and not na(posEntry)
    float lblY = posDir == 1 ? posEntry + nz(atr14, 0) * 1.5 : posEntry - nz(atr14, 0) * 1.5
    pRisk := box.new(bar_index, math.max(posEntry, posStop), bar_index, math.min(posEntry, posStop), border_color = color(na), bgcolor = POS_DD)
    // Written as `if` rather than a ternary on purpose: a ternary whose branches
    // call a DRAWING function is the one shape in Pine where an unwanted object
    // can be created by the branch you did not take.
    pRwd1 := box(na)
    pRwd2 := box(na)
    if not na(posT1)
        pRwd1 := box.new(bar_index, math.max(posEntry, posT1), bar_index, math.min(posEntry, posT1), border_color = color(na), bgcolor = POS_G1)
    if not na(posT2)
        pRwd2 := box.new(bar_index, math.max(posEntry, posT2), bar_index, math.min(posEntry, posT2), border_color = color(na), bgcolor = POS_G2)
    pBody := box.new(bar_index, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry, border_color = POS_OPENL, border_width = 1, bgcolor = POS_OPENBG)
    pLead := line.new(bar_index, posEntry, bar_index, lblY, color = POS_OPENL, width = 1)
    pLbl  := label.new(bar_index, lblY, (posDir == 1 ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT"), color = POS_OPEN, textcolor = TXT_DARK, style = posDir == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, size = size.small, tooltip = (posDir == 1 ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT") + " open\n──────────────────\nEntry " + str.tostring(posEntry, format.mintick) + "\nStop  " + str.tostring(posStop, format.mintick) + "\nTP1   " + str.tostring(posT1, format.mintick) + "\nTP2   " + str.tostring(posT2, format.mintick) + "\nRisk  " + str.tostring(posDist * posQty, "#.##"))

if execShowPosBox and strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(pBody)
    box.set_right(pRisk, bar_index)
    box.set_right(pBody, bar_index)
    box.set_top(pBody, math.max(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bottom(pBody, math.min(posEntry, close))
    if not na(pRwd1)
        box.set_right(pRwd1, bar_index)
    if not na(pRwd2)
        box.set_right(pRwd2, bar_index)
    // The risk block tracks the LIVE stop, so it visibly collapses at breakeven.
    if not na(posStop)
        box.set_top(pRisk, math.max(posEntry, posStop))
        box.set_bottom(pRisk, math.min(posEntry, posStop))

// 🔴 THE TARGET BANDS ARE TORN DOWN ON THE CLOSE, AND NOT DOING THAT WAS A REAL
// BUG. They are painted at the FILL, from the entry all the way to the target,
// because that is the trade's plan — and until 2026-08-15 nothing ever removed
// them. So a trade that was stopped out for −1R after one bar left a full-height
// GREEN column running down to a previous-week low that price never went near.
// Aaron, reading his own chart: "price never goes down, but there is a big green
// bar. I'm confused." The drawing was claiming profit the P&L does not have.
// `mpc_strategy.pine` already had the rule in writing — *"every band comes from
// the strategy's own closed-trade log, at the price the engine REALLY filled —
// never a fib level it merely aimed at"* — and it was not carried across.
// **A plan and a result are two different pictures, and only one of them may be
// left on the chart.** What survives the close is the entry-to-real-exit band and
// the entry-to-worst-price band, both measured, neither aimed at.
// ⚠ WITH A PARTIAL, ONE BAND CANNOT DESCRIBE THE TRADE. The first target banks
// half and the runner exits somewhere else, so the band drawn is the RUNNER's
// exit and the first rung is not shown separately. A+ splits it into stacked
// bands per rung; that is more machinery than this file has. Read the split off
// the Strategy Tester's trade list.
if execShowPosBox and justClosed and not na(pBody)
    float exitPx = strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(strategy.closedtrades - 1) : close
    box.delete(pRwd1)
    box.delete(pRwd2)
    pRwd1 := box(na)
    pRwd2 := box(na)
    box.set_top(pBody, math.max(posEntry, exitPx))
    box.set_bottom(pBody, math.min(posEntry, exitPx))
    if not na(posWorst)
        box.set_top(pRisk, math.max(posEntry, posWorst))
        box.set_bottom(pRisk, math.min(posEntry, posWorst))

// One result, one colour. The band is what stops a two-tick scratch — which the
// breakeven buffer books on purpose — being filed as a full win.
if execShowPosBox and justClosed and not na(pLbl)
    bool  won = not na(closedR) and closedR > execBeBandR
    bool  be  = not na(closedR) and math.abs(closedR) <= execBeBandR
    color lc  = be ? POS_BE  : won ? POS_WIN  : POS_LOSS
    color ll  = be ? POS_BEL : won ? POS_WINL : POS_LOSSL
    label.set_color(pLbl, lc)
    label.set_text(pLbl, (posDir == 1 ? "▲ LONG " : "▼ SHORT ") + str.tostring(closedR, "#.##") + "R")
    label.set_tooltip(pLbl, (posDir == 1 ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT") + (be ? " breakeven" : won ? " won" : " lost") + "\n──────────────────\nResult " + str.tostring(closedR, "#.##") + "R\nEntry  " + str.tostring(posEntry, format.mintick) + "\nStop   " + str.tostring(posStop, format.mintick) + "\nTP1    " + str.tostring(posT1, format.mintick) + "\nTP2    " + str.tostring(posT2, format.mintick))
    line.set_color(pLead, ll)
    box.set_bgcolor(pBody, be ? color.new(#FF9800, 80) : won ? color.new(#26A69A, 70) : color.new(#EF5350, 70))
    box.set_border_color(pBody, ll)

// The entry triangles. `plotshape` is a GLOBAL-SCOPE call, so it cannot live in
// the block above — the fill edge is re-derived here from the same test the
// tracker uses, so a triangle can never appear on a bar the tracker did not treat
// as a fill. ⚠ Not redundant with the boxes: a scratch paints a risk block a few
// pixels tall and reads as no trade at all, which is exactly when you need to see
// where it opened.
plotshape(execShowPosBox and strategy.position_size > 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0, title = "Long entry",  style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.belowbar, color = POS_GREENB, size = size.small)
plotshape(execShowPosBox and strategy.position_size < 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0, title = "Short entry", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = POS_REDB,   size = size.small)

//============================================================
//  BLOCKED SETUPS
//============================================================
// Only refusals from the ZONE onward are tagged. Codes 1-5 are "the sequence has
// not happened yet", which is the normal state of the market and would bury the
// five that are actually decisions. The tag reads the SAME `sBlk`/`lBlk` the gate
// chain wrote, so the tag and the diagnostic log can never disagree about why a
// trade did not happen.
var int lastTagKey = -1
int   tagCode  = sBlk >= 6 and sBlk <= 10 ? sBlk : lBlk >= 6 and lBlk <= 10 ? lBlk : 0
bool  tagShort = sBlk >= 6 and sBlk <= 10
float tagEdge  = tagShort ? sEntry : lEntry
if showBlockTag and tagCode > 0 and not armedNow and time_close >= timenow - debugDays * 86400000
    // Deduped on the leg, the code and the side: a setup refused for twenty bars
    // is one tag, but a CHANGED reason is a genuinely different refusal.
    int key = legId * 100 + tagCode * 2 + (tagShort ? 1 : 0)
    if key != lastTagKey
        lastTagKey := key
        label bl = label.new(bar_index, tagShort ? high : low, (tagShort ? "▼" : "▲") + " SETUP BLOCKED", style = tagShort ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = BLK_PINK, textcolor = TXT_DARK, size = size.small, tooltip = (tagShort ? "▼ SHORT" : "▲ LONG") + " blocked\n──────────────────\n" + f_blkWhy(tagCode) + "\n──────────────────\nLimit would have rested at " + str.tostring(tagEdge, format.mintick))

//============================================================
//  STATE PANEL — what the sequence is waiting for
//============================================================
// It reports the GATES rather than only the outcome, so a quiet market can be told
// apart from a rule set too tight — those need opposite responses.
// ⚠ It uses the TABLE palette, not the position one. They are different greens on
// purpose; `mpc_d_strategy.pine` crossed them and its winners drew in a table
// colour for weeks.
var table pbTbl = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 6, bgcolor = color.new(#1a1a1a, 10), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 70), border_width = 1)

f_row(int r, string k, string v, color vc) =>
    table.cell(pbTbl, 0, r, k, text_color = color.new(color.gray, 20), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(pbTbl, 1, r, v, text_color = vc, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)
    int _r = 0

if showStatePanel and barstate.islast
    int sd = dirDir
    f_row(0, "DIRECTION " + pbDirTf + "m", sd == 1 ? "bullish" : sd == -1 ? "bearish" : "none yet", sd == 0 ? TBL_OFF : TBL_GOOD)
    f_row(1, "SESSION", rawSess == 2 ? "New York" : rawSess == 1 ? "London" : "off-hours", rawSess == 0 or not sessTradable ? TBL_OFF : TBL_GOOD)
    f_row(2, "POOL " + (poolNm == "" ? "—" : poolNm), rawSess == 0 ? "—" : str.tostring(sd == 1 ? poolLo : poolHi, format.mintick), TBL_OFF)
    f_row(3, "SWEPT", rawSess == 0 ? "—" : (sd == 1 ? sweptLo : sweptHi) ? "yes" : "waiting", (sd == 1 ? sweptLo : sweptHi) ? TBL_GOOD : TBL_WARN)
    // In AT-THE-ZONE mode there are TWO waits behind one gate, and they need
    // opposite responses: price never reached the zone is a market fact, no shift
    // once it got there is a rule fact.
    bool cOk = sd == 1 ? confOkLong : confOkShort
    f_row(4, pbConfTf + "m SHIFT", not pbRequireConf ? "not required" : cOk ? "agreed" : confAtZone and not armTouched ? "waiting on the zone" : "waiting", cOk ? TBL_GOOD : TBL_WARN)
    f_row(5, "ZONE", pendDir != 0 ? "order resting" : strategy.position_size != 0 ? "in a trade" : f_blkWhy(sd == 1 ? lBlk : sBlk) == "" ? "ready" : f_blkWhy(sd == 1 ? lBlk : sBlk), pendDir != 0 or strategy.position_size != 0 ? TBL_GOOD : TBL_WARN)
